    "field": "Tropical expansion",
    "problem": "The subtropical jet shows weak and inconsistent poleward trends, contradicting the robust tropical expansion measured by other metrics; a discrepancy potentially caused by inaccurate jet-locating methods or high natural variability, which this paper investigates by introducing a new method based on the tropopause gradient.",
    "method": "The paper proposes the tropopause gradient method to locate the subtropical jet by identifying the peak gradient in potential temperature along the dynamic tropopause, which is defined as a surface of constant potential vorticity.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the weak poleward shifting trends of the subtropical jet by introducing a new method for its detection, and then examining its trends and variability to understand why they are smaller than other tropical expansion metrics.",
